  "stage": "study-review",
  "summary": "The expansive study of the 1962 First Sunday of Advent passes source review across all eleven appointments and both interpretations, each with its own four senses, and the revised Gospel and Offertory match the wording and punctuation of Lasance and Walsh, printed pp. 104\u2013105. On the difficulty in Romans 13:11, Chrysostom\u2019s Homily 24 supports the runner\u2019s increased effort as the prize draws near, while Aquinas, Super Romanos 13, lect. 3 [86224], explicitly distinguishes Paul\u2019s appeal for readiness from the Church\u2019s Advent use of the verse to voice those who awaited Christ\u2019s birth (print layout outside this review)."
}
